# Global AI Behavior Rules (Roo Code)

## Architectural Scope
- This is a mono-repo AI lab with multiple isolated experiments.
- `infra/` contains shared always-on services (reverse proxy, databases).
- `projects/` contains isolated experiments, each with its own docker-compose.yml.
- `shared/` contains reusable assets across experiments.
- `scripts/` contains DevOps and maintenance utilities.
- **Critical:** Do NOT modify files in `infra/` when working on an isolated project in `projects/` unless explicitly asked. Shared services are off-limits to individual experiments.

## File Creation Rules
- New experiments MUST be scaffolded from `projects/_template/`.
- All API keys and secrets go in `.env` files, NEVER hardcoded.

## Secret Management
- Never write plain-text API keys, tokens, or passwords into source files.
- Reference variables from the root `.env` file or project-specific `.env` files.
- Use `${VAR_NAME}` syntax in docker-compose files, never hardcoded values.

## Execution Safety
- Before executing shell commands, verify whether you are operating locally or on the remote Hetzner server.
- Prefer modifying `docker-compose` files over running manual one-off terminal tweaks.
- Always prefer `docker compose` (v2 plugin) over `docker-compose` (v1).
- Never run destructive commands (`rm -rf`, `docker system prune -a`) without confirmation.
- Never delete production data without confirmation.

## Coding Standards
- JavaScript/TypeScript: 2-space indentation, semicolons, single quotes.
- Python: Black formatter, 4-space indentation, type hints required.
- Shell scripts: `set -euo pipefail` at the top of every script.
- Dockerfiles: Multi-stage builds, non-root user, `.dockerignore` required.
- Markdown: 2-space indentation, no trailing whitespace.

## Git Conventions
- Commit messages: present tense, imperative mood ("Add feature" not "Added feature").
- Branch naming: `feature/`, `fix/`, `experiment/` prefixes.
- No committing `.env` files, `.log` files, or database storage directories.
